ke Tim Duncan in New  York while he would have been a great  player he would have hated it like San  Antonio was perfect for him there so  that's why when I if you go in with  LeBron man you got to be all in and it's  coming at you in directions that you  don't even see it coming and and it's  like how do we create a story today  other than LeBron had an unbelievable  game last night that's secondary it's I  don't know Miz he's spending - you  playing too many minutes what's Kobe  really saying about LeBron and we're  gonna win championship it's there  because everybody has got to get a story  and it's got to be different  it's got to be tiring on these players  well no doubt and it's also it's what's  the redeeming value for you to be in  that atmosphere and as you know any  number of guys said to me off the record  are just in conversation if if the team  wins if there's success it's well it's  LeBron and if the team is somehow has  some shortcomings it's well it's the  supporting cast and which means you like  anybody who's not LeBron is the problem  it's the coach  it's the GM it's the supporting cast  it's the it's the second star who's not  enough of a second star and and I think  the great distinction here is that we've  now seen all of this play out we've seen  Chris Bosh go and have to transform  himself we've seen Kevin Love have to  transform himself we've seen Kyrie  Irving get beat up for what he is or he  isn't and don't you know that you're  playing with LeBron James and it's a  it's a different demand and the reality  is you know the players that I talk to  will tell us a LeBron has nothing to do  with that I'm not so sure about that  but the bulk of it does come from  Media and the wet and the perception  that we create talking to Ric Bucher  Bleacher Report Writer columnist why  doesn't anyone want to play with lebron  anymore as the title of his latest  column okay with that being said give me  the player that you think would want to  go into this